Bundled secret / sensitive-data detection rules
================================================

config/bundled-secret-rules.json is a PUBLIC-SOURCE secret / sensitive-data rule library.
It exists so the Sample Sanitizer and Pack Generator can run pattern-based secret detection
from patterns that are entirely public and permissively licensed — the Sample Sanitizer
publishes its reachable source for public review (see CLAUDE.md Hard Rules 25 & 29), so
nothing proprietary may ship in it. The library is bundled with the app: there is no network
fetch and no minimum platform version.

Every pattern in bundled-secret-rules.json is one of:

  1. Adapted from gitleaks — github.com/gitleaks/gitleaks — MIT License.
     (credential / API-key / token / connection-URI patterns, incl. the SaaS
     batch: DigitalOcean, Shopify, HashiCorp Vault, Terraform Cloud, Docker Hub,
     Linear, Databricks, New Relic, PyPI, PlanetScale, Doppler)

  2. Adapted from Microsoft Presidio — github.com/microsoft/presidio — MIT License.
     (PII / financial patterns: SSN, payment-card networks, routing number, and the
     European set: IBAN, EU VAT, national IDs / fiscal numbers for FR, DE, NL, PL, BE,
     PT, NO, DK, SE, IT, ES, UK, IE)

  3. A vendor-PUBLISHED credential format. Prefixes such as AKIA (AWS), sk- (OpenAI),
     sk-ant- (Anthropic), xoxb-/xoxp-/xapp- (Slack), ghp_/gho_/glpat- (GitHub/GitLab),
     AIza/ya29. (Google), SG. (SendGrid), the eyJ… JWT structure and the
     -----BEGIN … PRIVATE KEY----- block are documented public token shapes, encoded
     identically by every open secret scanner. They are not proprietary to any party.

The file is processed by src/secret-rule-filter.ts: each rule is classified
(literal / structural / numeric / structured) and low-precision patterns are dropped. The
library is authored to be usable, so all 64 rules survive that filter
(40 literal / 12 numeric / 5 structural / 7 structured).

